  "title": "Sample a polar quarter circle",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Sample a polar quarter circle",
    "name_source": "document",
    "description": "Radius 2 over angles [0,pi/4,pi/2] gives x=[2,sqrt(2),0],y=[0,sqrt(2),2]. The oracle uses analytic constants with absolute/relative tolerance 1e-12.\n\nRadius 2 over angles [0,pi/4,pi/2] gives x=[2,sqrt(2),0],y=[0,sqrt(2),2]. The oracle uses analytic constants with absolute/relative tolerance 1e-12.\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: frog.studio.formula.evaluation@1; compiled owned-value service.\nExpected:\noutput-x_values (array<f64>) = [2,1.4142135623730951,0]\noutput-y_values (array<f64>) = [0,1.4142135623730951,2]\noutput-error (i32) = 0\n",
